TASK 7 – AWS EC2 DEPLOYMENT OF TWENTY CRM

1. OBJECTIVE

The objective of this task was to launch and configure an AWS EC2 instance, install Docker and Docker Compose, deploy the Twenty CRM application using Docker Compose, configure the required network access, and verify that the application is accessible from a web browser.

2. AWS EC2 INSTANCE

The application was deployed on an AWS EC2 instance running Amazon Linux 2023.

Operating System: Amazon Linux 2023
Deployment Platform: AWS EC2
Application: Twenty CRM
Application Port: 3000
Protocol: HTTP
Containerization: Docker
Orchestration: Docker Compose

3. SSH CONNECTION

The EC2 instance was accessed remotely using SSH from Git Bash.

Command used:

ssh -i "jatin-crm-key.pem" ec2-user@<EC2-PUBLIC-DNS>

After connecting, the operating system was verified using:

cat /etc/os-release

The output confirmed:

NAME="Amazon Linux"
VERSION="2023"
ID="amzn"

4. ROOT ACCESS

Root access was obtained using:

sudo su -

The current user was verified using:

whoami

Output:

root

5. STORAGE VERIFICATION

Disk space was checked using:

df -h /

The EC2 instance has an 8 GB root disk.

During the deployment, disk usage was monitored because Docker images and the application repository require storage.

6. DOCKER INSTALLATION AND VERIFICATION

Docker was installed on the Amazon Linux EC2 instance.

Docker version was checked using:

docker --version

Output:

Docker version 25.0.14

Running containers were checked using:

docker ps

7. DOCKER COMPOSE INSTALLATION
Docker Compose was required to run the Twenty CRM application and its dependent services.

Docker Compose was installed at:

/usr/local/bin/docker-compose


docker-compose --version

Output:

Docker Compose version v5.5.0

8. TWENTY CRM REPOSITORY

The Twenty CRM repository was cloned into the EC2 instance.

Working directory:

/opt/twenty

Repository was cloned using:

git clone https://github.com/twentyhq/twenty.git

The repository was then entered using:

cd twenty

The Docker configuration was located at:

packages/twenty-docker

9. DOCKER COMPOSE CONFIGURATION

The Docker Compose configuration was found at:

/opt/twenty/twenty/packages/twenty-docker/docker-compose.yml

The Docker Compose file contains the following services:

1. Twenty CRM Server
2. Twenty CRM Worker
3. PostgreSQL Database
4. Redis

The Twenty CRM server uses port:

3000

10. ENVIRONMENT CONFIGURATION

The example environment file was copied using:

cp .env.example .env

The .env file was configured with the required database, Redis, server URL, encryption keys, and local storage settings.

Important configuration included:

TAG=latest

PG_DATABASE_USER=postgres
PG_DATABASE_PASSWORD=<configured-password>
PG_DATABASE_HOST=db
PG_DATABASE_PORT=5432
PG_DATABASE_NAME=default
REDIS_URL=redis://redis:6379

SERVER_URL=http://<EC2-PUBLIC-IP>:3000

ENCRYPTION_KEY=<generated-key>
FALLBACK_ENCRYPTION_KEY=<generated-key>

STORAGE_TYPE=local

11. ENCRYPTION KEY GENERATION

Random encryption keys were generated using OpenSSL.

Command used:

openssl rand -base64 32

Two random values were generated for:

ENCRYPTION_KEY
FALLBACK_ENCRYPTION_KEY

12. DOCKER IMAGES

The required Docker images were downloaded using:

docker-compose pull

The following images were downloaded:

twentycrm/twenty:latest
postgres:16
redis:latest

13. STARTING THE APPLICATION

The Twenty CRM application was started using:

docker-compose up -d

Docker Compose created the required:

- Docker network
- PostgreSQL volume
- Twenty server volume
- PostgreSQL container
- Redis container
- Twenty server container

14. VERIFYING CONTAINERS

The container status was checked using:

docker-compose ps

The final status showed:

twenty-db-1       Up (healthy)
twenty-redis-1    Up (healthy)
twenty-server-1   Up (healthy)

The Twenty server exposed:

0.0.0.0:3000->3000/tcp

This confirmed that port 3000 was mapped from the EC2 host to the Twenty CRM server container.

15. APPLICATION HEALTH CHECK

The application health endpoint was tested using:

curl http://localhost:3000/healthz

The response was:

{"status":"ok","info":{},"error":{},"details":{}}

This confirmed that the Twenty CRM application was running successfully.

16. AWS SECURITY GROUP CONFIGURATION

The EC2 Security Group was configured to allow inbound TCP traffic on port 3000.

Port:

3000

Protocol:

TCP

The port was required so that the Twenty CRM application could be accessed from outside the EC2 instance.

17. BROWSER ACCESS

After configuring port 3000 in the EC2 Security Group, the application was accessed through a web browser using:

http://<EC2-PUBLIC-IP>:3000

The Twenty CRM application opened successfully in the browser.

This confirmed successful external access to the application.

18. DOCKER STORAGE CHECK

Docker storage was monitored using:

docker system df

Disk usage was also checked using:

df -h /

The Docker images used for the deployment included:

twentycrm/twenty
postgres
redis

The storage usage was monitored because the EC2 instance has limited disk capacity.

19. ISSUES FACED AND SOLUTIONS

Issue 1: Docker Compose package was not available.

Command:

dnf install docker-compose-plugin -y

Result:

No match for argument: docker-compose-plugin

Solution:

Docker Compose was manually downloaded and installed using the official Docker Compose release.

Issue 2: Twenty CRM server initially became unhealthy.

Command used to start the application:

docker-compose up -d

Initially, the server reported:

dependency failed to start: container twenty-server-1 is unhealthy

Solution:

The server logs were checked using:

docker-compose logs --tail=100 server

The logs showed that the NestJS application successfully started.

The container was then verified using:

docker-compose ps

The final status showed:

twenty-server-1   Up (healthy)

Issue 3: Application was not initially accessible externally.

Solution:

Port 3000 was added to the EC2 Security Group inbound rules.

After this configuration, the application was successfully opened using the EC2 public IP and port 3000.

20. FINAL VERIFICATION

The following components were successfully completed:

EC2 Instance                 - Completed
Amazon Linux 2023            - Completed
SSH Connection               - Completed
Docker                       - Completed
Docker Compose               - Completed
Twenty CRM Repository        - Completed
Twenty CRM Docker Image      - Completed
PostgreSQL                   - Healthy
Redis                        - Healthy
Twenty CRM Server            - Healthy
Port 3000                    - Configured
Health Check                 - Successful
Security Group               - Configured
Browser Access               - Successful

21. CONCLUSION

Twenty CRM was successfully deployed on an AWS EC2 instance running Amazon Linux 2023.

Docker Compose was used to run the Twenty CRM application along with PostgreSQL and Redis.

The application health endpoint returned a successful response:

{"status":"ok","info":{},"error":{},"details":{}}

All required containers were verified as healthy.

Port 3000 was configured in the EC2 Security Group, and the Twenty CRM application was successfully accessed through the EC2 public IP address.

This task provided practical experience with AWS EC2, Amazon Linux, SSH, Docker, Docker Compose, PostgreSQL, Redis, Security Groups, application deployment, health checks, and troubleshooting.Version was verified using:
The Docker Compose package was not available through the Amazon Linux DNF repository, so Docker Compose was downloaded manually.


